    },
    "body": "Joint geometric bank learning improved bank loss but damaged retained single-source behavior. This adds an offline readout-only loss using actual native geometric codes/states as constants, omitting recurrent context autodiff while retaining occurrence-position gathering and global Copy/Period/Stop alias loss. The driver freezes context/inactive source bits and native context/configuration/table/tokenizer through all exports and reloads.\n\nThe executed128-row comparison selects64: fullCE1.327649→1.146199, single complete31→34/64 (six gains/three losses), bank0→1/64, fresh0/32. No completequerypair succeeds. Independent first-token analysis finds Copy-ranking progress (target topCopy9→20/64), rather than terminal-only improvement. Keep all candidates and negatives; no shared-session default promotion, general-chat, full-prefix or energy claim.\n\nValidation:13 focusedRust tests, optimized build andfmt pass on source1ca0ab19; source-bound full128 admission1204positive targets/finiteactiveR/noCgrad; independent admission6530 and saved outcome26736 checks pass. Exact130-file/267,705,347B SHA/set return. LinuxCPU existing Runpod48/noGPU; build352.335s, prep2.251s, broad6.321s, fit74.960s. Rawgradient/optimizer/native independentreplay and localBLAKE3 are unverified; Metal unavailable onLinux is notcounted. Queue statuses acknowledge compatibility and do not execute these tests.\n\nUpdates current state, evidence and roadmap toward stable text-derived cue-to-occurrence/query geometry with zero-term parity and matched information/access controls; no unchanged readout dose or shared-session edit.\n\nReferences #1552. References #1512.\n",
